{"slug":"nested-list-weighted-sum","title":"Numbers in Nested Lists","topic":"backtracking","difficulty":"easy","order":405,"tags":["recursion","parsing","nesting"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"A list inside a list is a smaller copy of the same problem","body":["A nested list such as `[1,[2,3],[[4]],5]` is a list whose items are numbers **or lists**. Handling an item that is a list is exactly the original problem again, only on a smaller piece of the text. So a recursive function that reads **one list** and calls itself whenever it meets `[` is the natural tool.",{"code":"def read_list(s, pos, depth):        # s[pos[0]] is the \"[\" of this list\n    pos[0] += 1\n    total = 0\n    while s[pos[0]] != \"]\":\n        if s[pos[0]] == \",\":\n            pos[0] += 1\n        elif s[pos[0]] == \"[\":\n            total += read_list(s, pos, depth + 1)   # a smaller list\n        else:\n            start = pos[0]\n            while s[pos[0]] not in \",]\":\n                pos[0] += 1\n            total += int(s[start:pos[0]]) * depth\n    pos[0] += 1                                  # skip the \"]\"\n    return total"},"The position is shared by all calls (a list with one element in Python, a reference in C++, an array in Java), so that after an inner list returns, the outer call continues **after** it. The nesting depth of the text is the depth of the recursion, which is why the nesting is limited to 400 here."]},"statement":["A nested list is written with square brackets and commas; its items are integers or nested lists, for example `[1,[2,3],[[4]],5]`. The items of the outermost list have depth 1, the items of a list inside it have depth 2, and so on. Print the sum of every integer multiplied by its depth."],"inputFormat":["The only line has the nested list. It has no spaces. The outermost item is a list."],"outputFormat":["Print the weighted sum."],"constraints":["2 <= length of the line <= 4000","-10^6 <= every integer <= 10^6","Lists can be empty. The nesting is at most 400 levels deep."],"examples":[{"input":"[1,[2,3],[[4]],5]\n","output":"28\n","note":"1*1 + (2 + 3)*2 + 4*3 + 5*1 = 28."}],"hints":["Write a function that reads one list: it starts after a [ and stops after the matching ].","When you meet another [, call the same function with a depth larger by one.","Keep the reading position where all calls can see it, so an outer call continues after an inner list."],"starter":{"python":"s = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["`read_list` reads the items of one list. An integer adds `value * depth`; an opening bracket calls the function for the inner list with `depth + 1`. The shared position makes the outer list continue right after the inner one."],"complexity":"Time O(length), space O(nesting depth).","code":{"python":"def read_list(s, pos, depth):\n    pos[0] += 1\n    total = 0\n    while s[pos[0]] != \"]\":\n        if s[pos[0]] == \",\":\n            pos[0] += 1\n        elif s[pos[0]] == \"[\":\n            total += read_list(s, pos, depth + 1)\n        else:\n            start = pos[0]\n            while s[pos[0]] not in \",]\":\n                pos[0] += 1\n            total += int(s[start:pos[0]]) * depth\n    pos[0] += 1\n    return total\n\ns = input().strip()\n\nprint(read_list(s, [0], 1))\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long readList(const string& s, int& pos, int depth) {\n    pos++;\n    long long total = 0;\n    while (s[pos] != ']') {\n        if (s[pos] == ',') {\n            pos++;\n        } else if (s[pos] == '[') {\n            total += readList(s, pos, depth + 1);\n        } else {\n            int start = pos;\n            while (s[pos] != ',' && s[pos] != ']') pos++;\n            total += stoll(s.substr(start, pos - start)) * depth;\n        }\n    }\n    pos++;\n    return total;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    int pos = 0;\n    cout << readList(s, pos, 1) << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long readList(String s, int[] pos, int depth) {\n        pos[0]++;\n        long total = 0;\n        while (s.charAt(pos[0]) != ']') {\n            if (s.charAt(pos[0]) == ',') {\n                pos[0]++;\n            } else if (s.charAt(pos[0]) == '[') {\n                total += readList(s, pos, depth + 1);\n            } else {\n                int start = pos[0];\n                while (s.charAt(pos[0]) != ',' && s.charAt(pos[0]) != ']') pos[0]++;\n                total += Long.parseLong(s.substring(start, pos[0])) * depth;\n            }\n        }\n        pos[0]++;\n        return total;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        System.out.println(readList(s, new int[] {0}, 1));\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"[1,[2,3],[[4]],5]\n","output":"28\n"},{"input":"[]\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"[5]\n","output":"5\n"},{"input":"[[]]\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"[-7]\n","output":"-7\n"},{"input":"[[[-1]]]\n","output":"-3\n"},{"input":"[1,[],2,[[]],3]\n","output":"6\n"},{"input":"[[[[-100654,406297,-890126]],[],240899],[],[],667697,-352130,374774]\n","output":"-1165793\n"},{"input":"[[[[2873,215188,-115656],-980542,-99801],793261,[-717513]],573875,[-2065],-123705,-620248,[[-446882],12417,[359972,[[],460878,[]],657147]],-574322,782241]\n","output":"215342\n"},{"input":"[286542,[[[[[910225],278345,878499],955818],[932119,-416794,542867]]],237605,485731,835051,495670,[[-955586,[],-482525],420